# dev-only build artifacts — not shipped (kept on disk for dev, out of the prod repo)
# NB: `docs/plans/*`, not `docs/plans/` — git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a `!` re-include below it can never fire. Excluding the contents
# instead is what makes the negation on the next line work at all.
docs/plans/*
# ...except the rebuild plans. A plan is the review baseline: the recheck pass greps
# its Deferred list and rules findings blocking against its Verification Plan, and both
# report clean against a plan git cannot see — a criterion can then be softened with no
# diff to read. Tracking costs nothing here: the wheel packages only src/bad_research
# (pyproject `[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel] packages`), verified 0 docs/ entries in
# the built wheel, so this exclusion never affected what ships. `docs/superpowers/plans/`
# is already tracked, so this also restores consistency rather than setting a precedent.
!docs/plans/2026-09-*.md
docs/investigation/
docs/INTERFACES.md
docs/INTERFACES_KEYLESS.md
docs/KEYLESS_REBUILD_PLAN_OUTLINE.md
docs/SPEC.md
docs/enhancements/

# research vault — per-run output/scratch (eval + real runs), never shipped.
# ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. A bare `research/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, and it was silently swallowing `skills/research/` — the entire research skill,
# its SKILL.md and all eight lane recipes, invisible to git while looking committed.
# Same failure class as an unanchored `reference/` that once hid a shipped skill's docs.
/research/
